Package: BDCN
Title: Bayesian Dynamic Count Networks
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ying", "Wu", role = "aut"),
    person("Sheng", "Jiang", email = "jiangsheng@cuhk.edu.cn",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
  )
Description: Fits Bayesian dynamic count network models for edge-indexed
    multivariate count time series. The implementation combines a finite-shape
    negative-binomial approximation, Polya-Gamma augmentation, dynamic latent
    factors, graph-informed global-local shrinkage, posterior diagnostics,
    joint decoupled shrinkage and selection, and sequential one-step
    prediction. A reproducible sparse multi-hop propagation simulation is
    included, together with a frozen 24-edge Divvy bike example supporting
    arbitrary known calendar covariates and an all-pairs candidate domain.
